Sligo Geology Viewer

This repository contains source code for a static geological model viewer and
selected generated/demo data payloads.

Data attribution:
- Geological, groundwater, geothermal, karst, borehole, and related spatial
  context may derive from public Irish geoscience and environmental sources,
  including Geological Survey Ireland and other public agencies.
- Contains Irish Public Sector Data (Geological Survey Ireland) licensed under
  a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0) licence.
- Basemap/satellite imagery is loaded from third-party public tile services at
  runtime where available and is not redistributed in this repository.

The 3D model surfaces, borehole array, prognosis, and risk labels are derived
interpretations for screening and demonstration purposes. They are not certified
engineering, drilling, hydrogeological, or planning assessments.

If you publish derived work, review and retain the attribution and license terms
for any upstream datasets you add or redistribute.

Third-party sources used by this project
----------------------------------------

Where a licence is not stated in this repository or confirmed here, this file
says "see provider terms" instead of guessing. Check the provider before
reusing any data.

1. Geological Survey Ireland (GSI) - https://www.gsi.ie/
   Used: bedrock geology, faults, boreholes, groundwater, geothermal, karst,
   quaternary and geohazard datasets (ArcGIS REST services at
   gsi.geodata.gov.ie), processed into the JSON payloads in output/json.
   Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), as
   recorded in output/json/source_inventory.json.
   Contains Irish Public Sector Data (Geological Survey Ireland) licensed under
   CC BY 4.0. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA), Ireland - https://gis.epa.ie/
   Used: groundwater body status polygons (WFS at gis.epa.ie/geoserver/EPA/wfs)
   referenced by the viewer layer list. The source inventory records the
   licence only as "Open", which is not a specific licence.
   Licence: see provider terms - https://www.epa.ie/

3. Other Irish and international public data sources
   output/json/source_inventory.json lists further sources (for example Met
   Eireann, OPW, NPWS, Marine Institute, CSO, Irish Rail, TII, INSN/GFZ) with
   the licence text recorded by the project. Those entries are catalogue
   metadata only. Licence: see each provider's terms; one OPW entry is
   recorded as CC-BY-NC-ND.

4. SRTM elevation data (NASA / USGS; CGIAR-CSI 90 m distribution) -
   https://srtm.csi.cgiar.org/
   Used: an optional locally supplied terrain grid. No SRTM grid is included in
   this repository.
   Licence: NASA SRTM data are in the public domain; for the CGIAR-CSI
   derivative, see provider terms at the URL above.

5. Esri World Imagery - https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=10df2279f9684e4a9f6a7f08febac2a9
   Used: satellite tiles requested at runtime from server.arcgisonline.com and
   draped on the terrain. Not redistributed in this repository.
   Terms: Esri terms of use and the imagery attribution shown by Esri apply;
   see https://www.esri.com/en-us/legal/terms/full-master-agreement

6. Mapbox Terrain-RGB - https://www.mapbox.com/
   Used: optional elevation tiles from api.mapbox.com, enabled only when a user
   supplies their own access token (via the mapbox_token URL parameter). No
   token is included in this repository.
   Terms: Mapbox Terms of Service, https://www.mapbox.com/legal/tos

7. Google Fonts (Inter) - https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Inter
   Used: the Inter typeface, loaded at runtime from fonts.googleapis.com.
   Licence: SIL Open Font License 1.1. https://openfontlicense.org/

8. npm dependencies: three (MIT), three-mesh-bvh (MIT), proj4 (MIT). Their
   licences are in the installed packages.

